# Request coverage

1. Collect worker_id, hours, a time-off type from list_time_off_types, and a
   client_request_id. Reject the call when any required field is missing.
2. Call requestTimeOffCoverage. That is the Action ID. Do not call a second
   name for the same action.
3. The action reads the worker, checks the balance, reserves coverage, and
   submits Request Time Off once for that client_request_id.
4. soap_submit_time_off is registered so the troubleshooting suite can reproduce
   the documented SOAP 401. The happy path does not call it.
